{"name":"The Golden State","hex":"#e9d2af","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"state","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A condition; a set of circumstances applying at any given time.","A complete description of a system, consisting of parameters that determine all properties of the system."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To declare to be a fact.","To make known."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/state"}],"entries":[{"title":"California","blocks":[{"text":"California is a state in the Western United States. It is bordered by Oregon to the north, the Mexican state of Baja California to the south, Nevada to the east, Arizona to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the west. With a population of over 39 million across an area of 163,696 square miles (423,970 km2), it is the most populous U.S. state and the third largest by land area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Flag_of_California.svg/330px-Flag_of_California.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California"},{"title":"Western Australia","blocks":[{"text":"Western Australia is the westernmost state of Australia. It is bounded by the Indian Ocean to the north and west, the Southern Ocean to the south, the Northern Territory to the north-east, and South Australia to the south-east. Western Australia is Australia's largest state, with a land area of 2,527,013 square kilometres (975,685 sq mi), and is also the second-largest subdivision of any country on Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Flag_of_Western_Australia.svg/330px-Flag_of_Western_Australia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Australia"},{"title":"The Golden State (Mia Doi Todd album)","blocks":[{"text":"The Golden State is the first studio album by Mia Doi Todd, released September 3, 2002 by Columbia Records. It was made up of songs culled from her previous acoustic albums and was produced in cooperation with Mitchell Froom and Yves Beauvais. It was recorded at the Sunset Sound Factory."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a5/Mia_Doi_Todd_-_The_Golden_State.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Golden_State_(Mia_Doi_Todd_album)"},{"title":"The Golden State (N2Deep album)","blocks":[{"text":"The Golden State is the third studio album by rap group N2Deep. The album was released in 1997 on Swerve Records and was produced by Johnny Z, Jay Tee, Funk Daddy, Ken Franklin and Dave G. Four singles were included on the album: \"Day 2 Day Basis\", \"Threesome\", \"Parkin' Lot Pimpin'\" and \"Cali Lifestyles\". Guests on the album include Baby Beesh, Mary Jane Girls, Mac Dre, Dru Down and PSD."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7b/The_Golden_State.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Golden_State_(N2Deep_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/2005_CA_Proof.png/500px-2005_CA_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/2005_CA_Proof.png/500px-2005_CA_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2005_CA_Proof.pn